# Logs and performance
diag.title = Logs and performance
diag.desc = Measure temperature, CPU, battery and FPS in games; technical logs to investigate problems.
diag.measure = Measurement
diag.perf = Performance log in games
diag.perf.desc = During each game, records every 10 s the CPU frequency, the limit in force, temperature and battery, and a session summary at the end. Files in TriMuxData/logs/perf (open in a spreadsheet). Use it to compare profiles, 2.0 GHz and emulators. When off, nothing is written.
diag.fps = Show FPS in games
diag.fps.desc = Shows frames per second in a corner of the screen during the game (a RetroArch feature). Useful to check that a more economical profile still runs at full speed.
diag.sessions = Recorded sessions
diag.sessions.desc = Summary per profile (temperature, battery drain, CPU) and the list of the latest sessions.
diag.sessions.none = No sessions recorded. Turn the performance log on and play for a few minutes.
